# test

Reserved for future PlatformIO tests.

No automated tests are included in `v0.1.0`; validation is currently performed
with firmware builds and physical checks on the Waveshare target hardware.

## Manual valve API checks

Use the current node IP printed after WiFi connects.

1. Reboot the ESP32 and confirm `GET /valves/8` returns `"state":"closed"`.
2. Send `PUT /valves/8` with `{"state":"open"}` and confirm relay CH8 activates.
3. Send `GET /valves/8` and confirm `"state":"open"`.
4. Send `PUT /valves/8` with `{"state":"closed"}` and confirm relay CH8 deactivates.
5. Send `PUT /valves/8` with `{"state":"bad"}` and confirm HTTP 400.
6. Send `PUT /valves/8` with `{}` and confirm HTTP 400 with `missing_state`.
7. Send `GET /valves/1` and confirm HTTP 404.
8. Confirm `GET /outputs` and `PUT /outputs/relays/1` still work.
9. Confirm relays 1 through 7 do not change during valve 8 commands.
10. Confirm `session_active` is true while valve 8 is open and false after it closes.
11. Confirm `last_session_l` keeps the closed-session total after valve 8 closes.
12. Confirm `POST /flowmeter/reset-hydrological-year` resets `hydrological_year_l`.
